    pr_ref:  # 45f8
    description: "FOUND 2026-11-17. `./scripts/auto-pr --gov --detach` on a diagnostic pull request (#2228) ended in `governance_pending` and left `.git/PR_PENDING` holding \"2228\", as designed. `./scripts/merge-pr close 2228 --reason ...` then closed the pull request (exit 0, \"PR #2228 closed\") and LEFT THE GATE FILE: `test -f .git/PR_PENDING` was still true, so the pre-work check (\"if the file exists, wait for auto-pr to complete\") would have held every later task on a pull request that no longer exists. `auto-pr gov-cleanup 2228` is no way out: it refuses a pull request that is not merged (\"is not yet merged. Merge it first\").\n\nWHAT I DID: confirmed with `ci-debug pr-status 2228` (State: closed, Merged: False), then removed the file by hand and deleted the branch (local and remote).\n\nWHAT IS WANTED: `merge-pr close N` removes `.git/PR_PENDING` when the file names N, and deletes the branch as a merge does (or says that it does neither). scripts/merge-pr is a governance file: this needs the owner's approval before a pull request.\n\nThe `close` path's own header says \"This script does NOT create PR_PENDING — it only cleans it up\" (scripts/merge-pr:20); the two `rm -f` sites are on the merge paths only (lines 282 and 391 on dev eec3215e6)."  # 45f8
    fields: {}  # 45f8
